# Deploy to Vercel on GitHub push

Whenever the user asks to push changes to GitHub (including "push", "push this branch", or a diff-tab push action), also update Vercel production after a successful push.

Do this in the same turn:

1. Push the branch as requested (do not create extra commits unless asked).
2. From the repo root, deploy production with `vercel --prod --yes` using the already-linked `true-breeds` project.
3. If the deploy fails, fix the cause when it is a build/config issue we introduced, then redeploy.
4. Report the production URL (`https://www.truebreeds.com`) and deploy status.

Do not skip the Vercel deploy just because GitHub already had the commits, GitHub is not connected for auto-deploy, or the push reported "Everything up-to-date". If they asked to push, still deploy the current working tree to production unless they explicitly say not to.
